/* paint-composite: keep Chrome's layerization stable frame to frame (no visual change). */
/* 1. The 4 price cards float with a composited `translate` animation. Without a paint
      boundary around them, their moving layers force a full re-layerization
      (PaintArtifactCompositor::Update / "Layerize") on almost every frame of the page,
      even while the section is far off-screen. contain:paint gives them a fixed clip.
      Clip edge = padding box of the section; nothing inside paints past it. */
#pricing { contain: paint; }
/* 2. The status dots pulse by growing a box-shadow ring 0 -> 10px. A growing shadow
      changes the dot's visual rect each frame, which also forces a full re-layerization.
      A second, fully transparent ring fixed at the maximum extent keeps the visual rect
      constant; the visible ring is exactly the original one. */
@keyframes pulse {
  0%, 100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(177, 18, 18, 0.55), 0 0 0 10px rgba(177, 18, 18, 0); }
  70%      { box-shadow: 0 0 0 10px rgba(177, 18, 18, 0), 0 0 0 10px rgba(177, 18, 18, 0); }
}
@keyframes pulseGreen {
  0%, 100% { box-shadow: 0 0 8px #57F287, 0 0 0 0 rgba(87, 242, 135, 0.45), 0 0 0 9px rgba(87, 242, 135, 0); }
  70%      { box-shadow: 0 0 8px #57F287, 0 0 0 9px rgba(87, 242, 135, 0), 0 0 0 9px rgba(87, 242, 135, 0); }
}

